@flexiarg math-formalization/stamp-siblings-from-one-compiled-branch
@title Stamp Symmetric Branches from One Compiled Branch
@keywords Lean, cases, symmetry, branch, template, compile, repetition
@audience lean-provers
@tone heuristic
@provenance retro-promotion pass (2026-08-16), source memory e-19ae2af6-d067-4ab2-b401-d8c52cf10018

! conclusion:
  In a finite symmetric case split, make one branch compile end-to-end before
  reproducing its structure in the sibling branches.

  + context: Several cases share the same proof shape up to a small rotation,
    permutation, or renamed boundary condition.

  + HOWEVER: Confirm the symmetry really preserves every hypothesis. Do not copy
    a branch whose endpoint convention, sign, or type-class instance differs.

  + THEN: Choose a representative branch, resolve all API and elaboration issues
    there, extract its stable proof skeleton, and stamp the siblings with only the
    symmetry-specific data changed. Compile each stamped branch immediately.

  + BECAUSE: The first complete branch pays the API-discovery cost once; later
    branches become controlled mechanical variations instead of parallel experiments.

  + NEXT-STEPS:
    next[Choose the representative branch.]
    next[Compile it end-to-end.]
    next[Identify and verify every symmetry-specific substitution.]
